What would be a unique username that includes the words "Crazy" and "Cat" from a database of registered usernames?
Assuming a SQL database named "usernames" with a table named "registered" that includes a column "username", the following query can be used to check if a username containing those words already exists:
SELECT * FROM registered WHERE username LIKE '%Crazy%' AND username LIKE '%Cat%';
If no matching username is found, a new username can be generated and inserted into the database using the following SQL code:
DECLARE @new_username varchar(255);
SET @new_username = 'CrazyCat' + CAST((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM registered WHERE username LIKE 'CrazyCat%') AS varchar(10));
INSERT INTO registered (username) VALUES (@new_username); 
This code generates a new username by appending a count of existing usernames that start with "CrazyCat" to the end of the base username "CrazyCat". It then inserts the new username into the "registered" table.

