To determine the noun or name that "her" refers to in the sentence, we need to first identify the noun or name that "her" is replacing. In this case, "her" is replacing a person or object that was previously mentioned in the sentence or context. 
One way to approach this problem using Java is to use a natural language processing library like Stanford CoreNLP. Here's an example code snippet that uses CoreNLP to identify the noun or name that "her" refers to:
```
import edu.stanford.nlp.simple.*;
String sentence = "Mary gave the book to her.";
// Create a new CoreNLP pipeline
StanfordCoreNLP pipeline = new StanfordCoreNLP();
// Use the pipeline to annotate the sentence
Annotation document = new Annotation(sentence);
pipeline.annotate(document);
// Get the sentence's parse tree
Tree tree = document.get(CoreAnnotations.SentencesAnnotation.class).get(0).get(TreeCoreAnnotations.TreeAnnotation.class);
// Find the subtree that corresponds to "her"
Tree herSubtree = null;
for (Tree subtree : tree) {
    if (subtree.label().value().equals("PRP") && subtree.firstChild().label().value().equals("FW")) {
        herSubtree = subtree;
        break;
    }
}
// Find the noun or name that "her" refers to
String referent = "";
if (herSubtree != null) {
    Tree parent = herSubtree.parent(tree);
    for (Tree sibling : parent) {
        if (sibling != herSubtree && sibling.label().value().equals("NP")) {
            referent = sibling.firstChild().value();
            break;
        }
    }
}
// Replace "her" with the referent
String correctedSentence = sentence.replace("her", referent);
System.out.println(correctedSentence);
```
This code uses the `StanfordCoreNLP` library to annotate the sentence and parse it into a tree structure. It then searches the tree for the subtree that corresponds to "her" (which is identified as a pronoun with a foreign word as its child), and finds the noun or name that it refers to by looking at its parent and siblings in the tree. Finally, it replaces "her" with the referent and prints the corrected sentence ("Mary gave the book to Mary" in this case). 
