To create the table, you can use nested loops to generate all possible three-step arithmetic operations using the given set of numbers. Here is an example PHP code that does this:
```
<?php
$numbers = array(3, 5, 1, 4);
$operations = array("+", "-", "*", "/");
$table = array();
// Generate all possible three-step arithmetic operations
foreach ($numbers as $num1) {
  foreach ($numbers as $num2) {
    foreach ($numbers as $num3) {
      if ($num1 != $num2 && $num1 != $num3 && $num2 != $num3) {
        foreach ($operations as $op1) {
          foreach ($operations as $op2) {
            $expression = "$num1 $op1 $num2 $op2 $num3";
            $result = eval("return $expression;");
            if (!in_array($expression, $table) && is_numeric($result)) {
              $table[] = $expression;
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
// Filter and sort the table
$prime_table = array();
foreach ($table as $expression) {
  $result = eval("return $expression;");
  if (is_prime($result)) {
    $prime_table[$expression] = $result;
  }
}
arsort($prime_table);
// Display the table
echo "<table>";
echo "<tr><th>Expression</th><th>Result</th></tr>";
foreach ($prime_table as $expression => $result) {
