To extract key points from the article on "Biden Outlines Plan to Reform Immigration" and summarize it in the format of Mark down, you can use Java libraries such as Jsoup and Stanford CoreNLP. Jsoup can be used to extract the relevant text from the article, and Stanford CoreNLP can be used to perform natural language processing tasks such as sentence splitting, tokenization, and part-of-speech tagging.
To analyze the tone and sentiment of the article towards immigration reform, you can use Java libraries such as Sentiment Analysis API and Stanford NLP Sentiment Analysis. These libraries can analyze the text and provide a sentiment score indicating whether the tone of the article is positive, negative, or neutral towards immigration reform.
Here is an example Java code snippet that uses Jsoup and Stanford CoreNLP to extract key points from the article and summarize it in the format of Mark down:
```
import org.jsoup.Jsoup;
import org.jsoup.nodes.Document;
import edu.stanford.nlp.pipeline.StanfordCoreNLP;
import edu.stanford.nlp.ling.CoreAnnotations.SentencesAnnotation;
import edu.stanford.nlp.ling.CoreAnnotations.TextAnnotation;
import edu.stanford.nlp.util.CoreMap;
import java.util.Properties;
public class ImmigrationSummary {
  public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
    // Extract text from the article using Jsoup
    Document doc = Jsoup.connect("https://www.nytimes.com/2021/02/18/us/politics/biden-immigration-reform.html").get();
    String text = doc.select("article").text();
    // Create a Stanford CoreNLP pipeline
    Properties props = new Properties();
    props.setProperty("annotators", "tokenize, ssplit, pos");
    StanfordCoreNLP pipeline = new StanfordCoreNLP(props);
    // Perform natural language processing on the text
    String summary = "";
    for (CoreMap sentence : pipeline.process(text).get(SentencesAnnotation.class)) {
      String sentenceText = sentence.get(TextAnnotation.class);
      if (sentenceText.contains("legal immigration") || sentenceText.contains("illegal immigration") || sentenceText.contains("asylum-seeking") || sentenceText.contains("refugee resettlement")) {
        summary += "- " + sentenceText + "\n";
      }
    }
    // Print the summary
    System.out.println(summary);
  }
}
```
Note that this code snippet only extracts sentences containing the relevant keywords and concatenates them into a bullet-pointed summary. It does not perform any sentiment analysis.

